- use of marks or signs to imply sponsorship, affiliation or endorsement;
- extraction of protected material to build a substitute product or a misleading representation of the framework;
- patent rights, trade-secret rights or access to private layers.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS

By submitting material through a Pull Request, Issue or another public project channel, the contributor represents, to the extent reasonably required, that they have the right to submit it and are not deliberately disclosing secrets, credentials, sensitive personal data or third-party material without sufficient permission.

Contributors retain the rights they hold in their contributions. To enable review, traceability, preservation and integration, the contributor grants Pedro Martínez Alhambra / Innova_N a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission of sufficient duration to preserve project genealogy and to reproduce, store, adapt, integrate, display and distribute an accepted contribution within the repository, NEOCore™, WEB4™, documentation and other official Innova_N projections, while preserving attribution and provenance where materially identifiable.

This integration permission does NOT automatically transfer authorship or imply truth, canonisation, `NC-CR-*` credit, payment, equity, sovereignty or voting rights.

If you cannot grant these permissions, state the restriction clearly BEFORE submitting the material so that it can be evaluated without assuming rights that do not exist.

4. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Third-party text, quotations, images, datasets, code or other materials retain their own rights and licences. Their presence in the repository does not expand the original permissions. Attribution and provenance must be preserved.

5. MARKS AND NAMES

The names Innova_N, NEOCore™, Open Synthesis™, Neodialectica Framework™ / Network, WEB4™ and other names identified as project marks or signs are not licensed by this notice for uses implying origin, sponsorship, certification or affiliation. Descriptive or nominative uses permitted by law are not restricted by this clause.

6. NO WARRANTY

Content is provided for reading, scrutiny and project development "as is", without a general warranty of fitness for a particular purpose, freedom from error or final validation. The canon is open and reopenable; traceability is not validation.

7. SCOPE DOUBTS

If a translation, file or context appears to grant broader rights than another without an unambiguous specific licence, the broader permission must not be inferred automatically. Consult the relevant rights holder or raise a licensing question before reuse outside the scope above.
